'.source.gfm, .text.md':
  '- [ ] github task':
    'prefix': 'lia-task'
    'body':   '- [${1: }] ${2:line with Markdown}'
    'description': """
      Task lists use the GitHub-flavoured Markdown syntax: a list item that starts with [ ] (open) or [X] (done). Users can check and uncheck the boxes. If the course version is 1.0.0 or higher, the states are stored persistently in the browser.

      Example:
        - [ ] This is not checked by default
        - [X] This one is checked by default
        - [ ] Tasks can contain __Markdown__
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://liascript.github.io/course/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/liaScript/docs/master/README.md'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">📋</span>'

  '- [ ] github task ... <script>...</script>':
    'prefix': 'lia-task-js'
    'body':   """
      - [${1: }] ${2:task-definition}
      - [${3: }] ${4:task-definition}
      <script output="${5:tasks}">"@input"</script>

      <script>
        let tasks = @input(`${5:tasks}`)
        ${6:tasks.every(done => done) ? "All done!" : "Keep going ..."}
      </script>
    """
    'description': """
      A script directly after a task list runs every time a box is checked or unchecked, but its result is not shown. Give it an output="name", then other scripts on the same slide can read the states with @input(`name`) and react to them. The value is an array of booleans, one per task, e.g. [true, false].

      Example:
        - [X] Biology
        - [ ] Chemistry
        <script output="tasks">"@input"</script>

        <script style="width: 100%">
        try {
          let task = @input(`tasks`)

          if (task[0]) {
            send.liascript(`## Biology

        Hey, great, you want to learn something about Biology.

        * resource 1
        * resource 2`)
          } else send.clear()
        } catch(e) { }
        </script>
    """
    'descriptionMoreURL': 'https://liascript.github.io/course/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/liaScript/docs/master/README.md'
    'leftLabelHTML': '<span style="color:#ff0">📋</span>'
